steps:
Step 4 — Add the missing CSS classes that LocalLoginScreen.tsx already references but index.css does not define. These classes must be added to index.css. The auth-screen already has a basic definition; augment it and add the two-column split layout below it:
  .auth-screen { min-height:100vh; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 420px; } (at ≥900px — keep existing radial-gradient background)
  .auth-intro { display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; padding:64px 72px; color:#4d4560; }
  .auth-intro h1 { font:500 clamp(28px,3.5vw,44px)/1.1 'Playfair Display',serif; color:#4d4560; letter-spacing:-.03em; margin:12px 0 16px; max-width:480px; }
  .auth-intro p { color:#857c91; font-size:13px; line-height:1.7; max-width:380px; margin:0 0 24px; }
  .auth-brand { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; font:600 18px 'Playfair Display',serif; color:#4d4560; margin-bottom:32px; }
  .auth-feature-list { display:flex; gap:20px; margin-top:8px; }
  .auth-feature-list span { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; font-size:12px; color:#8c8199; }
  .auth-visual { position:relative; width:260px; height:260px; margin-top:40px; }
  .auth-grid-lines { position:absolute; inset:0; background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(147,134,170,.12) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(147,134,170,.12) 1px,transparent 1px); background-size:32px 32px; border-radius:50%; }
  .auth-orbit { position:absolute; border-radius:50%; border:1px solid; animation:spin linear infinite; }
  .auth-orbit-one { width:180px; height:180px; top:40px; left:40px; border-color:rgba(163,140,185,.35); animation-duration:18s; }
  .auth-orbit-two { width:120px; height:120px; top:70px; left:70px; border-color:rgba(163,140,185,.25); animation-duration:12s; animation-direction:reverse; }
  @keyframes spin { to { transform:rotate(360deg); } }
  .auth-signal { position:absolute; bottom:20px; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); display:flex; align-items:flex-end; gap:3px; height:30px; }
  .auth-signal span { width:4px; border-radius:2px; background:#a393be; animation:signalBounce 1.2s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .auth-signal span:nth-child(1) { height:30%; animation-delay:0s; }
  .auth-signal span:nth-child(2) { height:65%; animation-delay:.15s; }
  .auth-signal span:nth-child(3) { height:45%; animation-delay:.3s; }
  @keyframes signalBounce { 0%,100% { opacity:.4; transform:scaleY(.6); } 50% { opacity:1; transform:scaleY(1); } }
  .auth-card-mark { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; margin-bottom:20px; }
  .auth-status { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; font-size:11px; color:#83ab9a; }
  .auth-status i { display:inline-block; width:6px; height:6px; border-radius:50%; background:#83ab9a; animation:statusDot 2s ease-in-out infinite; }
  At ≤900px: .auth-screen { grid-template-columns:1fr; } and .auth-intro { display:none; } so only the card shows on mobile.

Step 5 — Add missing classes for the workspace launchpad launch-icon variants and the header kicker dot, which are referenced in Home.tsx JSX but undefined in CSS:
  .launch-icon { width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:14px; display:grid; place-items:center; flex-shrink:0; }
  .launch-template { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8e1f2,#d5cae8); color:#6b5d89; }
  .launch-voice { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f2dfe4,#e8c9d4); color:#8c5a68; }
  .launch-connect { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#dceee7,#c8e0d4); color:#3d7a66; }
  .workspace-launchpad button em { display:block; font-size:11px; font-style:normal; color:var(--muted-foreground); margin-top:2px; }
  .header-kicker { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; }
  .header-kicker-dot { display:inline-block; width:6px; height:6px; border-radius:50%; background:#b8a8c8; animation:statusDot 2s ease-in-out infinite; }
